Kyanite's code is free software. The name "Kyanite" and this logo are not:
all rights in the designs and files in this repository are reserved.

You may reproduce the logo, unmodified, to refer to Kyanite — an article, a
talk, documentation, a list of links, a package repository that distributes
Kyanite, a screenshot of a machine running it. That is nominative use, and it
needs no permission. Pick the variant that suits your background rather than
recolouring, and keep the proportions.

You may not use the name or the logo to name, brand or sign anything that is
not the Kyanite project; modify the logo and still call it the Kyanite logo;
imply an endorsement that does not exist; or register either as a trademark,
domain or account name that would be taken for the project itself.

Build your own image from the free code as much as you like — that is the
point of releasing it. But it is your project: give it its own name and its
own mark. You may say truthfully that it is based on Kyanite.

The word in the logotype is set in Inter, by Rasmus Andersson, under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1. Inter is not covered by the reservation above; its own
licence applies, and it permits derivative works.

For anything outside this, ask.
